ent, I didn’t realize that was the case.  I wasn’t looking to add a breaking change and I’m glad you pointed it out. I’ll see what I can do to come up with something that maintains the existing semantics while also fixing the race.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-10-17T10:41:58Z\\n\\nWe have been discussing this in yesterday's SIG meeting, and have decided this fix is incorrect and the current behavior is the proper one.\\n\\nSee https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588#issuecomment-3414917592\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i also disagre that folk should do this themselv especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist for other instrument such a otelecho i think this discuss would be better synchron though if you re abl to i d recommend you to join our next sig meet tomorrow at 4pm utc http github com open telemetri communiti tab readm ov file implement sig nicksherron 2025 10 14t08 48 08z i disagre with this be a violat of go s convent in the context of the middlewar pattern we don t flow forward at the end of a middlewar we go back to it parent i also disagre that folk should do this themselv especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist for other instrument such a otelecho i think this discuss would be better synchron though if you re abl to i d recommend you to join our next sig meet tomorrow at 4pm utc http github com open telemetri communiti tab readm ov file implement sig ok well one thing is for certain you all have a much better understand of the exist pattern and user expect for this project than i do it s get quit late for me so i ll sleep on this and give your point their time to marin a far a the sig meet go that s a great idea and sound fun too unfortun that s a fair busi time for me but i ll do my best to make it nicksherron 2025 10 14t08 59 49z especi sinc this ha been the default behavior for mani year now and the same behavior exist