motive-dev-operator/pull/260\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"2025 06 10t14 53 31z cross referenc by dmathieu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 7456 2025 06 16t07 32 18z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 2025 06 16t07 40 13z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6903 2025 09 18t16 17 38z mileston by mralia v1 39 0 2025 10 16t20 42 15z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri semant convent pull 2296 2025 11 03t09 39 05z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 2025 11 03t14 23 56z cross referenc by dmathieu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 8107 2025 12 04t18 17 39z demileston by mralia v1 39 0 2025 12 04t18 17 39z mileston by mralia v1 400 2025 12 19t13 23 07z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri semant convent pull 3228 2026 01 12t17 33 42z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8386 2026 01 13t15 23 09z close by pellar 2026 04 27t06 41 51z cross referenc by coderabbitai bot http github com cento automot suit automot dev oper pull 260\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"00a9e2d2b5ea8cde\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3264205142022739, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11401570314610558, \"vector_similarity\": 0.82203174, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n### Description\\n\\n`otelhttp` only uses `span.RecordError(err)` when `errType` is not empty\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/otelhttp/transport.go#L132-L140\\n\\nBut `ErrorType` method never returns an empty attribute.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8/instrumentation/net/http/httptrace/otelhttptrace/internal/semconv/httpconv.go#L443-L458\\n\\n### Expected behavior\\n\\nI don't have a preference on whether we should record `error.type` with `exception.type` at the same time. But the comment and the logic here seem conflicted. \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7254  \\n\\n**Author**: XSAM  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-04-23T02:21:22Z · **Updated**: 2026-01-13T15:23:09Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed (completed)  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelhttp  \\n\\n**Milestone**: v1.40.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Discussion (15)\\n\\n**dmathieu** — 2025-04-23T08:03:12Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 descript descript otelhttp onli us span recorderror err when errtyp is not empti http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http otelhttp transport go l132 l140 but errortyp method never return an empti attribut http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob b8572491f2d143672581d1c51693c928d376dff8 instrument net http httptrace otelhttptrac intern semconv httpconv go l443 l458 expect behavior i don t have a prefer on whether we should record error type with except type at the same time but the comment and the logic here seem conflict sourc id src issu 02 issu otelhttp can not record error for span when produc new semant convent open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 7254 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7254 author xsam creat 2025 04 23t02 21 22z updat 2026 01 13t15 23 09z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close complet label bug area instrument instrument otelhttp mileston v1 400 discuss 15 dmathieu 2025 04 23t08 03 12z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"67607a2c8d579c3a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31762658639439134, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09651329484913052, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8335576, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\nI also think that stabilization of https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans is a blocker for v1 of `otelhttp`. \\n\\n@open-telemetry/go-maintainers, do any thoughts or other proposals?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**dashpole** — 2025-11-03T14:55:36Z\\n\\nWould your proposed guidlines be in-line with the current Development spec, or are you proposing something new?  If they are in-line with that spec, then SGTM.  Otherwise, I would prefer if you updated the spec first so our instrumentation libraries don't get out ahead of the spec.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T15:00:09Z\\n\\n> Would your proposed guidlines be in-line with the current Development spec, or are you proposing something new?\\n\\nI want them to be following the current semantic conventions that are in Development\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-02]\\n\\n# Issue: otelhttp: Cannot record error for spans when producing new semantic convention (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#7254)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://g