, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2988874144902368, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08731907641462398, \"vector_similarity\": 0.79254687, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"My proposal is to not use `span.RecordError` for **terminating errors** per [recording errors on spans semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans).\\n\\nDuring the SIG meeting, it was also noted that `span.RecordError` captures a stack trace. However, since the stack trace reflects where the error was recorded, not where it originated, I don’t find it particularly valuable. Additionally, capturing and emitting a stack trace has a performance cost. In most languages with exception handling (such as Java or .NET), the stack trace is already included in the thrown exception so the cost of capturing the stack trace was already taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the exception was thrown.\\n\\n> @pellared does that mean span.RecordError should essentially never be called by instrumentation, since panic recovery is already handled by the SDK? Almost makes it seem like we should deprecate RecordError in the API,\\n\\nI believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nWhile instrumentation libraries typically just return errors, they could also benefit from `span.RecordError` if the underlying library provides hooks into retry or failure logic. In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via `span.RecordError` gives users better visibility into transient issues **without prematurely ending the span**.\\n\\nFor these reasons, I don’t think `span.RecordError` should be deprecated. It might be worth capturing these use cases in the [error recording semantic conventions](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md) (cc @lmolkova).\\n\\nSide note: There is an OTEP https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/pull/4333 that proposes to record exceptions/errors as log records instead of span events.\\n\\n>  and document that End should handle recording exceptions for panics.\\n\\nI think that documenting that `span.End` should handle recording exceptions for panics is a good idea.\\n\\nIn my opinion, this is how we implement [recording an exception](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/exceptions.md#recording-an-exception) in the most possible user-friendly way.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"my propos is to not use span recorderror for termin error per record error on span semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span dure the sig meet it wa also note that span recorderror captur a stack trace howev sinc the stack trace reflect where the error wa record not where it origin i don t find it particular valuabl addit captur and emit a stack trace ha a perform cost in most languag with except handl such a java or net the stack trace is alreadi includ in the thrown except so the cost of captur the stack trace wa alreadi taken and the stack trace is taken in the place where the except wa thrown pellar doe that mean span recorderror should essenti never be call by instrument sinc panic recoveri is alreadi handl by the sdk almost make it seem like we should deprec recorderror in the api i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error while instrument librari typic just return error they could also benefit from span recorderror if the under librari provid hook into retri or failur logic in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span for these reason i don t think span recorderror should be deprec it might be worth captur these use case in the error record semant convent http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md cc lmolkova side note there is an otep http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif pull 4333 that propos to record except error a log record instead of span event and document that end should handl record except for panic i think that document that span end should handl record except for panic is a good idea in my opinion this is how we implement record an except http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace except md record an except in the most possibl user friend way\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"085f95b8d9b42db9\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29880967739439135, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09651329484913052, \"vector_similarity\": 0.77083457, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_count\": 9, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:22\", \"token_count\": 4323, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nOr, should we record this error?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.RecordError(err)\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\nI don't think we should just ignore the error without recording it in the span. `RecordError` has `semconv.ExceptionMessage(err.Error())` to record error message, which is always useful when debugging.\\n\\nAre you trying to limit the usage of `RecordError` to only instrumentation? Why can the instrumentation record the error message?\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-04T15:12:11Z\\n\\n> For instance, when facing code like this,\\n\\nIt looks like a **terminating** error to me which falls into https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans:\\n\\n> When the operation ends with an error, instrumentation:\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:38:55Z\\n\\nI see. So, your proposal is\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\\n\\tspan.SetAttributes(semconv.ErrorType(err))\\n\\n\\tspan.SetStatus(codes.Error, err.Error())\\n\\n\\treturn err\\n\\n}\\n\\nreturn nil\\n\\n```\\n\\nIt makes sense.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-08-05T06:40:03Z\\n\\nCorrect \\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-05T06:50:03Z\\n\\n> In such cases, recording retry attempts as span events via span.RecordError gives users better visibility into transient issues without prematurely ending the span.\\n\\nWould it be strange to say we only record `exception` events when `panic` and retriable error happens? Retriable errors do not seem to be categorized as a type of `exception`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-11-03T13:34:57Z\\n\\nMy plan is to add OTel Go specfic \\\"recording errors\\\" guidelines into our [Style Guide](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md#style-guide). Maybe it should be part of some more public user-facing docs like https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, I prefer first trying it out more internally. One of the reasons is that https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-spans is \\\"Development\\\" and would need to be \\\"Stable\\\" first. I would work on it on the scope of:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"return err return nil or should we record this error go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span recorderror err return err return nil i don t think we should just ignor the error without record it in the span recorderror ha semconv exceptionmessag err error to record error messag which is alway use when debug are you tri to limit the usag of recorderror to onli instrument whi can the instrument record the error messag pellar 2025 08 04t15 12 11z for instanc when face code like this it look like a termin error to me which fall into http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span when the oper end with an error instrument xsam 2025 08 05t06 38 55z i see so your propos is go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil span setattribut semconv errortyp err span setstatus code error err error return err return nil it make sens pellar 2025 08 05t06 40 03z correct xsam 2025 08 05t06 50 03z in such case record retri attempt a span event via span recorderror give user better visibl into transient issu without prematur end the span would it be strang to say we onli record except event when panic and retriabl error happen retriabl error do not seem to be categor a a type of except pellar 2025 11 03t13 34 57z my plan is to add otel go specfic record error guidelin into our style guid http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go blob main contribut md style guid mayb it should be part of some more public user face doc like http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev i prefer first tri it out more intern one of the reason is that http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on span is develop and would need to be stabl first i would work on it on the scope of\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"062966a1a409f1ea\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], 