\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"id\": \"6fd777f3e87a494f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29776047961801316, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.046527828025733076, \"vector_similarity\": 0.88397, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"875c049e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-7427.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 37741, \"chunk_count\": 26, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:02\", \"token_count\": 14705, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"---\\n\\n**pellared** — 2025-06-16T07:44:04Z\\n\\nI created \\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/7470\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6904\\n\\n- https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6903\\n\\nI think it might be also good to add some \\\"error recording\\\" recommendations in https://pkg.go.dev/go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace. However, we should first clarify it on the semantic conventions side.\\n\\n>  I believe [`span.RecordError`](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-specification/blob/main/specification/trace/api.md#record-exception) remains valuable, particularly for **non-terminating errors**. A common use case is **retry logic**, where errors occur but don't immediately end the span. This is especially relevant in the context of **custom instrumentation**, where developers have full control and can explicitly record such intermediate errors.\\n\\nThis seems not compliant with https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/blob/main/docs/general/recording-errors.md#recording-errors-on-metrics\\n\\n> Errors that were retried or handled (allowing an operation to complete gracefully) SHOULD NOT be recorded on spans or metrics that describe this operation.\\n\\nCurrently, the only use case I see the only use of `span.RecordError` to use it for \\\"unhandled exceptions\\\" (which for Go can be done in the SDK) and to record multiple errors like here:\\n\\nhttps://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/blob/9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go#L119-L124\\n\\nI do not find the semantic conventions clear and probably some work is also needed there.\\n\\nCC @lmolkova\\n\\n---\\n\\n**XSAM** — 2025-08-03T20:45:58Z\\n\\nSorry for joining the discussion late.\\n\\n@pellared I am confused about what we should do to handle errors, especially **non-terminating errors**. Should we do nothing if we encounter an error?\\n\\nFor instance, when facing code like this, do we do nothing for the error we receive?\\n\\n```go\\n\\nctx, span := tracer.Tracer(instrumentationName).Start(ctx, \\\"example\\\")\\n\\ndefer span.End()\\n\\nerr := query(ctx, db)\\n\\nif err != nil {\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"pellar 2025 06 16t07 44 04z i creat http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 7470 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6904 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6903 i think it might be also good to add some error record recommend in http pkg go dev go opentelemetri io otel trace howev we should first clarifi it on the semant convent side i believ span recorderror http github com open telemetri opentelemetri specif blob main specif trace api md record except remain valuabl particular for non termin error a common use case is retri logic where error occur but don t immedi end the span this is especi relev in the context of custom instrument where develop have full control and can explicit record such intermedi error this seem not compliant with http github com open telemetri semant convent blob main doc general record error md record error on metric error that were retri or handl allow an oper to complet grace should not be record on span or metric that describ this oper current the onli use case i see the onli use of span recorderror to use it for unhandl except which for go can be done in the sdk and to record multipl error like here http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib blob 9e39469c07651d62d1acd5155ddf9843c1b63436 instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go l119 l124 i do not find the semant convent clear and probabl some work is also need there cc lmolkova xsam 2025 08 03t20 45 58z sorri for join the discuss late pellar i am confus about what we should do to handl error especi non termin error should we do noth if we encount an error for instanc when face code like this do we do noth for the error we receiv go ctx span tracer tracer instrumentationnam start ctx exampl defer span end err queri ctx db if err nil\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"id\": \"edc3ac974ee2a669\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2969199594146429, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07744332773520408, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8090321, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8745fc628a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-7254.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 15479, \"chunk_